# 🎯 [Agent name]

**Frontmatter guide:**
- `name` — identifier matching the `<domain>-<purpose>` pattern and the agent's folder name (e.g., `technical-writer`, `code-analyzer`)
  - **Format:** hyphens match skill names, which the Agent Skills spec requires; the [Claude Code subagent docs](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents) only forbid `:` and cap names at 256 characters
- `description` — one sentence saying when Claude should delegate to this agent, since Claude Code decides from it alone
- `tools` — comma-separated allowlist of only the tools the job needs (e.g. add `Write` only if it writes files) — leaving it out grants every tool
- `model` — `inherit` (use the session's model), or an alias such as `sonnet`, `opus` or `haiku`, which never goes stale the way a full model ID does
- `isolation` — `worktree`, the only value, runs the agent in its own git worktree, so leave it out for a read-only agent
- **Other fields:** Claude Code ignores unrecognised fields without an error, so add one only for people reading the file

**Metadata header** (straight after the frontmatter): `version`, `created`, `updated`, each an HTML comment such as `<!-- version: 1.0.0 -->`.

