## Creating your agent — Next steps

1. **Fill in frontmatter** — name, description, tools and model, then the version/created/updated header
2. **Write Purpose** — one-liner value prop
3. **Write When to use** — concrete scenarios + NOT use cases
4. **Write Role & Principles** — persona (3-5 lines) + 5-7 core principles
5. **Write Constraints** — explicit boundaries (what agent does NOT do)
6. **Create evals.yaml** — scenarios covering its main triggers and one case where it shouldn't fire

**See also:** `on_demand/claude_config/authoring_guidelines.md`, in your Claude config directory, for the full creation guidelines and hard gates.

---

## Quality checklist

Before finalizing:
- [ ] Frontmatter complete (name, description, tools, model, and isolation if the agent changes files)
- [ ] Metadata header straight after the frontmatter (version, created, updated)
- [ ] Purpose: one-liner, non-technical, user-focused
- [ ] When to use: 3+ concrete scenarios + 2+ NOT use cases
- [ ] Role: 3-5 lines describing persona
- [ ] Principles: 5-7 core behavioral guidelines
- [ ] Constraints: explicit boundaries (what agent does NOT do)
- [ ] Total length: ~40-60 lines (lean, scannable)
- [ ] evals.yaml created, covering the main triggers and one case where it shouldn't fire

**Resources:**
- Full guidance and hard gates: `on_demand/claude_config/authoring_guidelines.md`, in your Claude config directory
- Testing: `on_demand/testing/_testing_design_pattern.md`, in your Claude config directory
